remotix-install — the REMOTIX installation engine

One program: it installs, checks, certifies and uninstalls REMOTIX. It carries the CATALOG of the
supported combinations inside it, and the catalog is updated with this package
(`remotix-install catalog` shows it).

Updates
  REMOTIX comes as one file, remotix-VERSION.run (DECISIONS §10.36): to update, run the new one
  (sudo sh remotix-VERSION.run): it shows the plan with the exact packages and asks. No archive is
  added to the system. After a version change the package scripts run `remotix-install post-upgrade`,
  which records the versions and says whether the installation is still certified.

REMOTIX does not change the system: what it needs and is missing (a desktop, a driver, a repository,
an open port) `remotix-install check` says, and providing it is up to the administrator.

Trust: the .run file is checked with the sha256 published on the REMOTIX site; inside, the payload
checks itself too.
